Methylation preprocessing

This directory contains preprocessing scripts used to prepare transposable element (TE) insertion coordinates and sequences for the downstream methylation workflows.

These scripts do not calculate methylation directly. They convert RetroInspector-derived insertion information into the input formats required by the internal and regional methylation analyses.

Workflow overview

RetroInspector outputs
        |
        +--> insertion ID
        +--> chromosome
        +--> insertion breakpoint
        +--> inserted sequence (vcf_alt)
        |
        v
prepare_internal_TE_input.R
        |
        +--> internal_TE_input.tsv
        |       |
        |       +--> 01_internal_TE_methylation.sh
        |
        v
prepare_flanking_regions.R
        |
        +--> left.bed
        +--> right.bed
        +--> flanking_regions_map.tsv
                |
                +--> 02_regional_methylation.sh

prepare_internal_TE_input.R

Purpose

Prepares the four-column input table required for internal methylation profiling of non-reference TE insertions.

The script combines:

a table containing TE insertion loci and RetroInspector sequence identifiers; and

a RetroInspector insertion table containing the inserted sequence (vcf_alt).

The resulting file contains:

TE_ID    chromosome    insertion_position    insertion_sequence

The output is written without a header because it is consumed directly by 01_internal_TE_methylation.sh.

Usage

Rscript prepare_internal_TE_input.R \
    candidate_insertions.csv \
    retroinspector_insertions.rds \
    internal_TE_input.tsv

Required RetroInspector columns

The RetroInspector insertion table must contain:

seqId
vcf_alt

Supported formats are:

.rds
.tsv
.txt
.csv

Output

internal_TE_input.tsv

Example structure:

TE001    chr1    123456789    ACGTACGT...
TE002    chr8    87654321     GCTAGCTA...

The inserted sequence is subsequently incorporated into an insertion-specific custom reference by 01_internal_TE_methylation.sh.

prepare_flanking_regions.R

Purpose

Generates genomic windows surrounding RetroInspector-defined TE insertion breakpoints for regional methylation analysis.

For the analyses reported in the paper, 500-bp windows were generated immediately upstream and downstream of each insertion breakpoint.

The script produces BED-compatible regions that can be passed directly to 02_regional_methylation.sh.

Usage

Rscript prepare_flanking_regions.R \
    internal_TE_input.tsv \
    flanking_regions/ \
    500 \
    one_based

Arguments:

1. Input TE table
2. Output directory
3. Window size in bp
4. Coordinate mode: bed0 or one_based

Coordinate conventions

The coordinate convention must be specified explicitly.

Use:

one_based

when the insertion position is a 1-based genomic coordinate.

Use:

bed0

when the insertion position is already a 0-based BED-style breakpoint.

The output BED files always use standard 0-based, half-open BED coordinates.

For a BED breakpoint p and a window size w:

LEFT  = [p - w, p)
RIGHT = [p, p + w)

Coordinates extending below zero are truncated at chromosome position 0.

Outputs

left.bed
right.bed
flanking_regions_map.tsv

left.bed and right.bed contain the regions used by Modkit.

flanking_regions_map.tsv preserves the relationship between the original insertion coordinate and the generated BED windows, making coordinate transformations explicit and traceable.

Relationship to the methylation workflow

The preprocessing scripts feed the two main methylation workflows:

Internal TE methylation

prepare_internal_TE_input.R
        |
        v
01_internal_TE_methylation.sh

This workflow constructs insertion-specific custom references, realigns nanopore reads, and measures methylation within the inserted TE sequence.

Regional methylation

prepare_internal_TE_input.R
        |
        v
prepare_flanking_regions.R
        |
        v
02_regional_methylation.sh

This workflow calculates methylation in genomic regions flanking the insertion breakpoint. In the paper, 500-bp left and right windows were used.

When 02_regional_methylation.sh is run with Modkit in phased mode, its output can subsequently be used for both combined regional methylation and haplotype-resolved analyses.

Requirements

R
dplyr
readr
stringr

The exact software environment used for the study should be documented at the repository root, for example with:

environment.yml

Suggested repository location

scripts/
└── methylation/
    ├── preprocessing/
    │   ├── README.md
    │   ├── prepare_internal_TE_input.R
    │   └── prepare_flanking_regions.R
    │
    ├── 01_internal_TE_methylation.sh
    ├── 02_regional_methylation.sh
    │
    └── analysis/
        └── pairwise_methylation_statistics.R

The analysis/ directory should contain downstream filtering, pairwise methylation comparisons, descriptive statistics, and result-table generation, while preprocessing/ is restricted to preparing coordinates, sequences, and BED regions.
